{
 "description": "Shared cases for Formulon date serial conversion (C ABI fm_convert_*, JS Formulon.convert*, Python convert_*). Each row: id; direction (civil_to_serial | serial_to_civil); date1904 (bool); input; expect {c, js, py}; optional only (bindings that run the row). civil_to_serial input is {year, month, day, hour, minute, second}; serial_to_civil input is {serial} or {serial_string} (a string, type-error row). A numeric field given as a string stands for a non-finite or signed-zero number: \"NaN\", \"Infinity\", \"-Infinity\", \"-0\". An expect is {value: number | {year..second}} or {error: name, layer}. layer 1 = rejected inside the binding (RangeError / TypeError / ValueError) and never reaches C; layer 2 = FM_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT from C, surfaced by the binding as its InvalidArgument error. Valid civil rows equal =DATE(y,m,d)+TIME(h,mi,s) and valid serial rows equal YEAR()..SECOND() of the serial, in a workbook with the same date1904 setting. Python rows that cannot be built as a datetime (month 13, hour 24, year 0 or 10000) are excluded through only; 1900-02-29 is a ValueError there.",
